    "turn_text": "of legislation in play. Yeah, well, there's been a lot of attention toward the need to put limits on Congressmen and women trading stocks and to restrict that. And I'm certainly for that. And I've co-sponsored a couple bills that would have to do that. This is all about restoring the American people's trust in our government. And so I'm for that. But when we were looking at the landscape of things, a lot of the decisions that are made by our government that affect the American people are actually being made by the bureaucracy. And so you can just think through COVID the last couple of years, how many decisions were made that the American people had to live with that were based, met either medical decisions or even military decisions and systems that are being advocated for by the Pentagon, they were kind of getting no attention placed to them. Meanwhile, a number of those officials who are making decisions had stocks related to what they were overseeing. In some cases, would trade right before either regulations were put on a certain industry or regulations lifted from a certain industry. And it's very troubling to see that kind of thing happening. And so our bill was spent to make sure that the executive branch is held to that high standard as well. And we're talking senior level executive members. We're not talking about your local post office worker who isn't making those kind of decisions. But senior level executive branch members need to be held to that kind of sort of scrutiny as well to make sure that weapon systems that those decisions are being made, not based on somebody's stock portfolio or desire to get on the board of a major contractor after they retire, but that they're being made based on you know what's really in the strategic best interest in national security when it comes to medicines and foods and those kind of things the same sort of thing we need to make sure that you know we're approving those items that are really in the best interest not because somebody's stock portfolio is going to be benefited by a certain drug being approved and like and you know since we've introduced that bill the Wall Street Journal as has done, they did an article where they did a pretty in-depth study of the most in-depth study that we know so far of the executive branch and their stock portfolios and they found out some crazy things like Department of Defense officials had stock holdings in Chinese companies. And most Americans were kind of like, really? you should be removed from office for doing that. And so the fact",
